    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0147" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg27"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Beaupré to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-02-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Beaupré reports that a revolution started to-day in Buenos Aires and several
                    of the provinces. Arsenals and police stations were attacked simultaneously, and
                    some of them were taken with a view of seizing the arsenals and making prisoners
                    of the President and the cabinet ministers and to force them to resign. Vigorous
                    measures were taken, however, by the government and many arrests were made. The
                    city has been placed under martial law. Order will probably soon be
                    restored.</p>
            </div>
